{"kind":"stack","id":"s-sun-eyes","title":"Protecting our eyes from the sun","theme":{"background":"#fff8e7","foreground":"#1f2937","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Why can the sun be dangerous to our eyes?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"It sends out harmful light that can hurt our eyes","why":"Strong sunlight contains harmful rays that can damage eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"It makes our eyes grow bigger","why":"Pupils may think bright light changes eye size, but it does not.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"It makes our eyes change colour","why":"Pupils may mix up eye colour with eye damage from light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Sunglasses"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Glasses with dark lenses that block some of the sun's harmful light from reaching our eyes."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these protects our eyes from the sun?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Wearing a hat with a brim","why":"A brim shades the eyes from the sun overhead.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Staring straight at the sun","why":"Pupils may think looking longer helps, but it harms eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Closing our mouth tightly","why":"Pupils may confuse eyes with mouth; mouth closing does nothing for eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is the best time to be careful about strong sunlight?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The middle of a sunny day","why":"The sun is strongest around midday, so its harmful light is strongest then.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Early on a winter morning","why":"Pupils may think low winter sun is always strong, but midday is strongest.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Late at night","why":"Pupils may forget that sunlight is only strong during the day.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Sunscreen"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-e","content":"A cream for the skin that protects it from the sun's harmful light. It does not go in the eyes."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You are outside on a bright sunny day. Your friend says the sun is not strong today. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Put on sunglasses anyway","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Look at the sun to check how bright it is","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Your eyes stay comfortable and safe in the bright light. Well done for protecting them."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Looking at the sun can hurt your eyes. Always look away and protect your eyes instead."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which is the safest thing to do on a sunny day?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Wear sunglasses that block harmful light","why":"Sunglasses that block harmful light protect eyes from sun damage.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Look directly at the bright sun","why":"Pupils may think a quick look is harmless, but it can hurt eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Rub your eyes hard in the sunshine","why":"Pupils may think rubbing clears glare, but it does not protect eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"How many of our senses does our body use to notice bright light? Choose the right answer."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"One, our eyes","why":"Eyes are the only part of the body that sees light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Two, our eyes and our ears","why":"Pupils may think ears help with light, but they only hear sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Three, our eyes, nose and skin","why":"Pupils may think skin senses light, but only the eyes do.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"You finished the sun and eye safety stack!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Great work. Remember to wear sunglasses, a hat and never look straight at the sun."}],"actions":[]}}
